    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1849 Cottonwood became a stagecoach town, later growing into a major shipping point for cattle, lumber, and crops once the Southern Pacific Railroad reached it in 1872.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cottonwood%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in 1852, and a Bavarian immigrant Jacob Foster bought 240 acres in 1859 that now form the town center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
